      "final_message": "I rewrote `merge_intervals` in `solution.py` so it follows the README. Both public tests pass, and I ran a few extra edge-case checks, which also behaved correctly.\n\nWhat it does now:\n- **Input checks:**\n  - If `intervals` isn't a list, it raises `TypeError`.\n  - Each item must be a two-element list or tuple of plain ints (bools not accepted) with start \u2264 end, or it raises `ValueError`.\n- **Merging:** it sorts intervals by start and merges any interval that starts at or before the current merged end, so intervals that just touch are merged too.\n- **Output:** it returns a new list of `[start, end]` pairs and doesn't change the input list or its items. Empty input returns `[]`.\n\nThe extra checks covered unsorted mixed list/tuple input (left unchanged), empty input, touching intervals, bool, float and wrong-length items, and a tuple passed instead of a list.\n\nDONE: Rewrote merge_intervals to validate input, sort by start and merge overlapping or touching intervals into a new list without changing the input; public tests pass.",
